# Secrets & credentials — never commit
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.template
*.pem
*.key
*.priv
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
*.ppk
*.asc
*.gpg
*.pgp
id_rsa
id_ed25519
*.secret
secrets.*
credentials.json

# Wizard runtime directory — generated secrets.env, filled config, .setup-state
# (§7.7.2). Never commit. The committed secrets.env.example template is
# re-included below (the `secrets.*` rule above would otherwise swallow it —
# negation must come after it for gitignore last-match-wins).
prod/runtime/
!prod/config/secrets.env.example
.agents/memory-local/

# Redteam-multi regenerable scratch (M1-684). Each /redteam-multi run's durable
# audit record — verdict-*.txt, cross-examination.md, and any hand-written
# disposition.md — stays tracked; the bulk below is fully reproducible from the
# prompt template + diff (rendered prompts embed the whole diff + threat model),
# so it is kept out of permanent history. The redteam-multi.sh script still
# WRITES these into the run directory as working state — this only stops them
# being committed. Single-auditor /redteam evidence (docs/plan/m1/redteam/*.md)
# is one markdown file per audit and is unaffected.
docs/plan/m1/redteam-multi/**/prompt-*.txt
docs/plan/m1/redteam-multi/**/reply-*.txt
docs/plan/m1/redteam-multi/**/inv-*.txt
docs/plan/m1/redteam-multi/**/diff.patch
docs/plan/m1/redteam-multi/**/porcelain-*.txt
docs/plan/m1/redteam-multi/**/preflight.txt
